<title>NORWAY: Storebrand share up on 1996 result.</title>
<headline>Storebrand share up on 1996 result.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stock in Storebrand ASA, Norway's biggest insurance company, rose 3.74 percent in early trade on the Oslo bourse on Wednesday following the release of 1996 results.</p>
<p>The share was up 1.70 crowns at 47.20 crowns at 1020gmt.</p>
<p>Trade was brisk valued at nearly 30 million crowns.  </p>
<p>Group profits fell 13.6 percent to 1.25 billion crowns partly because of weaker non-life results. But financial portfolio gains helped offset some of the losses and the result beat market expectations.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
